# <Project name>   <!-- team-init sets this; the shift is announced with it -->

## Team process (agent-team plugin)

Role: engineering            # engineering | design
Profile: apple               # apple | web | none
Review model, high tier: session   # `session` = the session's model; name another (opus, fable) for every round of a high-tier review, the expensive choice, so it is the owner's
Plugin feedback: <channel>   # where a shift sends what it learned about the plugin, when there is something: 'SendMessage to the session named "<maintainer session name>", else an issue on <owner>/agent-team' (name the session as the app shows it; an id may not resolve, and a session may lack the tool); leave unset to send nothing
Shifts chain: yes   # a shift whose context runs out with work queued starts the next one itself (shift-start.sh); `no` leaves every start to the owner; `max N` allows N self-started shifts in a row (one shift can use a large share of a weekly limit)
Shift sessions: keep   # keep: ended shifts stay open in the app until the owner archives them, and the next start closes what was archived (an idle claude each meanwhile); close: shift-start.sh --close-ended closes them at once (the app archives them, readable)

Follow the `agent-team:team-process` skill for every piece of work; read it at session start.
Direction: `ROADMAP.md` (owner's). What is in flight: `.agent-team/state.md`. Structure: `ARCHITECTURE.md`. Design docs: `DESIGN.md`, `TOKENS.md`, `design/`.

